From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: fix(vpu): sync upstream v1.0.1 pm_runtime irq/reset ordering

The boot-hang seen on `.66` (and on the prior 7.0.x NEXT kernels) is a
hardware race in `mvx_pm_runtime_resume()`: `enable_irq(ctx->irq)` is
called BEFORE `reset_control_deassert(ctx->rstc)`.  At that point the
device is mid-reset: the IRQ can fire immediately after enable, dump into
a non-functional state, and the probe error path then deadlocks inside
the IRQ bottom half before any printk is ever produced.

The matching upstream CIX v1.0.1 (cixtech/cix_opensource__vpu_driver
branch cix_mainline_dev, commit 4080a85, released the day after the bug
was reported) reverses the order: deassert the reset, then enable the
IRQ.  Match the symmetric path in `mvx_pm_runtime_suspend()` by asserting
the reset before gating the clock off so the block is left quiescent.

This commit is the kernel-side fix (CI metal-verified prior).

The diff also folds in a 7.2 mainline compat fix (`del_timer` to
`timer_delete()` in `mvx_log_group.c`) that was missed by 0128's
<string.h> addition; the only other unmodified 0127/0128 hunk in the
prepared 0130 patch was the `q->num_buffers` to `vb2_get_num_buffers()`
swap which is already covered by 0126's `MVX_VB2_NUM_BUFFERS` macro.

The remainder of the prepared v1.0.1 sync (rrc_dqp feature work,
debugfs session memory tracking via `mvx_session_update_memory_stats`,
`sw_core_mask` rewrite of `mvx_hwreg.{c,h}`) was left OUT -- those hunks
depend on vendor-only CIX compat headers (`<linux/string_compat.h>`,
`<linux/v4l2_compat.h>`) and CIX-specific SCMI helpers
(`scmi_device_get_freq()`, `scmi_device_opp_table_parse()`, etc.)
that do not exist in Linux 7.2 mainline.  They are deferred to a
follow-up patch series once the 7.2 mainline SCMI/glue helpers the
upstream assumes are imported.
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c   | 17 +++++++---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/mvx_log_group.c |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
@@ -1119,6 +1119,11 @@ static int mvx_pm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
         mvx_switch_enpwoff(ctx, true);
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Match the resume path: assert reset BEFORE gating the clock off, so
+     * the block is left in a clean, quiescent state across the suspend.
+     */
+    reset_control_assert(ctx->rstc);
     if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(ctx->clk))
         clk_disable_unprepare(ctx->clk);
 
@@ -1160,11 +1165,15 @@ static int mvx_pm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
         return ret;
     }
 
-    enable_irq(ctx->irq);
-
-    reset_control_assert(ctx->rstc);
-    usleep_range(10, 20);
+    /*
+     * Order matters: deassert the reset BEFORE enabling the IRQ.  Otherwise
+     * the IRQ can fire mid-reset (when the device is not yet fully out of
+     * reset) and corrupt probe state, leading to a silent boot-hang before
+     * any printk.  This matches upstream cixtech/cix_opensource__vpu_driver
+     * v1.0.1 (commit 4080a85).
+     */
     reset_control_deassert(ctx->rstc);
+    enable_irq(ctx->irq);
 
     mvx_switch_qchannel_clock_gating(ctx, true);
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/mvx_log_group.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/mvx_log_group.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/mvx_log_group.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/mvx_log_group.c
@@ -295,7 +295,7 @@ void mvx_log_group_deinit(void)
         vfree(dur_buf);
     dur_buf = NULL;
 #if MVX_USE_UTILIZATION_TIMER
-    del_timer(&util_timer);
+    timer_delete(&util_timer);
 #endif
     mvx_log_group_destruct(&mvx_log_dev);
     mvx_log_group_destruct(&mvx_log_session_if);
-- 
